WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome to the show!
-Appreciate you having me.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.003
-Congratulations. You are
dressed like a champion,

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
may I say?
-Oh, yeah, you know...

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very dapper!
-I make suits for a living.

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:09.042
People don't know that about me.
-This is a suit you made?

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I made this.
Damari Savile is my company.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got a brick and mortar
in Philadelphia.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.713
-That -- this is very upsetting
to me that you're good

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:16.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
at another thing.
I don't -- I don't like that.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:20.353
So this was the second time that
you were a Super Bowl champion.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
You won with
the New Orleans Saints

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
your rookie year, which was,
of course,

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
their first Super Bowl ever,
as well.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what was it like being
a veteran

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.928 line:92%
compared to the experience?

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:32.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well that first one in 2009,
I was a rookie.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.134 line:92%
And my head was spinning.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we're getting ready
to play the Colts.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:38.405
Peyton Manning and the great,
you know, offense they had.

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:41.808
And I wasn't supposed to start.
I was a Special Teams guy.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:45.245
And the starter in front of me
got walking pneumonia, like,

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
two days before the game.
And I got thrown in

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:50.116
kind of the second half, and so
everything happened so fast.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't even get to enjoy it.
But this time around,

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.088
being a veteran, being a captain
of the team,

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:58.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
being a key contributor
and everything that led up

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.827 size:75% position:38%
to this year, it was
something different.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.362 size:88% position:44%
Be able to bring that to
the city of Philadelphia

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.865
is something that myself
and my family won't forget.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Fantastic. A couple of photos.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:11.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
There you are.
Again, far too well-dressed.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:14.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
But I have to say as when to

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
comes to well-dressed
in the family,

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is your daughter.
Is it Elle?

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Elle.
-So how old is Elle?

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.814
This is -- she was at the game.
-Elle just turned 4.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:21.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Aw!
-Fantastic.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:27.253
-She had her Eagle wings on.
-[ Laughs ] That's very cute.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know she -- in
the playoffs, she was, like,

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:32.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
"hey, Daddy's going
to the supermarket."

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.760 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.795 size:81% position:41%
But by the time we got
to Super Bowl Sunday,

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
she understood everything
that was going on.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.865
-That's great.
-"You just won the Super Bowl."

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.633
-Oh, that's very exciting.
And I guess that would be

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:41.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
a nice difference between your
rookie year and now, too,

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:45.205
is that you have someone to --
you have kids to share it with.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:47.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have two kids now, yeah.
I just had a daughter

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
three weeks ago, so, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:54.314
-Congratulations. Now I...
My dad's from Pittsburgh.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:56.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I grew up a Steelers fan.
And I was very happy

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.184
because now the Steelers,
at least for another year,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
still have
the most Super Bowl trophies.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:02.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-Your dad was a Giants fan

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:05.992
and held on to being a Giants
fan for a long time, right?

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.128 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, I mean, I grew up
in northern New Jersey,

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that's Giants,
you know, country.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.432
-Yeah.
-But he was looking for a reason

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
to give up on Eli Manning
and those guys, so...

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
When I got to New Orleans,

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
he obviously became
a Saints fan.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.007 size:78% position:39%
I came up to Philly,
and there was no way.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.409
He had to cut every tie
that he had to that team.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
He did it willingly
and, you know,

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
after those Super Bowl
commercials,

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.550
I think he's probably thinking,
"that was a great decision."

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

